# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Windows batch files are consumed by cmd.exe, which parses them by byte offset and
# resynchronizes on CR. Checked out with LF (or carrying a multi-byte UTF-8 character
# in a comment), cmd loses its place and executes the tail of a `rem` line as a
# command: the schedulers spent weeks printing "'m' is not recognized as an internal
# or external command" before anyone traced it. Keep .bat CRLF here, and keep their
# contents pure ASCII (no em dashes in comments) -- either alone can trigger it.
*.bat text eol=crlf
